   "version": "v0.5.23",
   "title": "A3 LR bracket passes (A2s and A3mx robust at 6e-3): C206-C208 back to VERIFIED; sandbox /proc gap confirmed and filed (SQ61)",
   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>A3 LR bracket passes: C206-C208 return to VERIFIED. The sandbox's /proc gap is confirmed and filed.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A3 amendment 1, final</strong> (registered v0.5.18; seed 5, 200M tokens, clean80; <code>experiments/checks/results/a3_assembled.json</code>, key <code>A3_amendment1_lr_bracket</code>):</li></ul><p>| Arm | 3e-3 | 6e-3 | 1.2e-2 | Best | 6e-3 vs best | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | A2s | 0.27291 | 0.27449 | 0.28367 | 3e-3 | +0.58% | | A3mx | 0.25333 | <strong>0.25176</strong> | 0.25793 | 6e-3 | 0 |</p><p>Both arms are LR-robust at 6e-3 by the registered rule (within 1% of the best), so <strong>C206 (ternary MoE core -3.3%), C207 (ternary cost splits evenly) and C208 (all-parts model's standing) return to VERIFIED</strong>. A3mx is at its best LR, so its +4.35% gap to the tuned E24 is not an LR artifact. A limitation is added: A2s's 3e-3 is 0.58% better, so effects against A2s may be overstated by up to about 0.6 points, and no decision changes.</p><ul><li><strong>Still running on the last box:</strong> A3 amendment 2 (A2f at 3e-3 / 1.2e-2), then A2 amendment 3 (E27 at 221.6M tokens, seeds 2-4).</li><li><strong>Quick review 14:47 (safety/sandbox):</strong> its <code>/proc</code> question was checked directly. Under the sandbox's <code>unshare -rnm</code>, a child sees all 32 host processes and can read every cmdline (no PID namespace). Filed as an SQ61 extension: <code>unshare -rnmpf --mount-proc</code> plus a fail-closed probe, with env/fd sentinel tests. C106's \"not a security boundary\" limitation stands. No model-generated code has been executed at scale, and Q14 stays human-blocked.</li></ul>"
