   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 14:09: the long-context result gets a positional control (SQ392, registered), three new side quests, and a FLOP-counter flag checked and rejected. Erratum: A3mx does not \"tie\" dense.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Outside review</strong> (<code>notes/reviews/2026-11-23-1409-review.md</code>, Haiku), triaged in its footer:</li><li><strong>Accepted:</strong></li><li>SQ392 (top pick): RoPE position interpolation on SQ351's dense checkpoints, to test whether GDN's -60.7% past 1,024 tokens is mostly unscaled-RoPE degradation. Its prediction is registered in PREDICTIONS.md: about -30% after interpolation, and the result is restated if it falls inside -30%.</li><li>SQ391: Mixture-of-Depths routing across loop passes, to design around loops' compute cost.</li><li>SQ393: bits-matched quality, ternary-wide vs fp16-narrow at equal weight bytes.</li><li><strong>Merged:</strong> sparse top-k coda retrieval into SQ383; same-shape A2f -&gt; A2s self-distillation into SQ356.</li><li><strong>Fixes:</strong> C208 gains a limitation that its 1.58-bit memory figures assume packing that has not been built (SQ378). The README's \"does not stack at 200M\" bullet now carries \"(C202, PARTIAL)\".</li><li><strong>Rejected after checking the code:</strong> the claim that the FLOP counter overstates truncated-BPTT arms. Logged run compute has counted no-grad passes as forward-only since v0.5.3 (<code>gogeta/train.py:345-346</code>), so C209's ~10% compute gap stands.</li><li><strong>Erratum (v0.5.17):</strong> \"the all-parts model ... ties dense per FLOP\" is wrong. TOST at +-1% (<code>experiments/checks/a3_tost.py</code>, <code>results/a3_tost.json</code>) gives A3mx vs E20 +1.10%, 90% CI [-0.13, +2.33], p = 0.58: <strong>equivalence not shown, and no advantage over dense shown</strong>. A3mx vs A2f (+1.36%) and vs E24 (+4.35%) are not equivalent either. Quick review 14:09 raised this.</li><li><strong>Fleet:</strong> the A3 amendment 1 LR bracket started on box 4 (A2s/A3mx at 3e-3). The 1.2e-2 pair is queued, and A4 continues on the other boxes.</li></ul>"
