   "title": "Claim audit 2026-11-23-1202: 35 claims, no downgrades (C203 Holm checked, C30 WRONG rejected); A1 holds at equal wall-clock",
   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Claim audit 2026-11-23-1202, plus quick reviews 12:01 (skeptical peer) and 12:04 (data engineer).</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Audit:</strong> 8 Codex auditors, all ok, reviewed 35 claims: 14 SOLID, 7 WEAK, 13 NEEDS-EVIDENCE, 1 WRONG. Each was checked against primary files. <strong>No downgrades.</strong></li><li><strong>C203 WEAK (Holm adjustment), rejected after computing it:</strong> the four registered E60 comparisons have |t| = 21.0, 24.8, 10.0 and 14.2 (df 10.3, 10.0, 7.8, 5.0), so each p &lt; 2e-4, under Holm's 0.0125 for m = 4. The t-statistics are recorded as evidence; VERIFIED stands.</li><li><strong>C30 WRONG, rejected:</strong> Ouro Table 13's OlympiadBench row reads 76.44 at T = 4 and 39.26 at T = 8, exactly as claimed. The auditor read SuperGPQA's row.</li><li><strong>Confirmed, limitations added:</strong> C93 (its stale \"no multi-seed 200M model\" note is updated) and C74, C35, C76, C75, C38 (paper-reported scope).</li><li>The 13 NEEDS-EVIDENCE verdicts are on claims already UNVERIFIED.</li><li><strong>A1 table labels (12:01 review):</strong> the parenthesised pairs in v0.5.4's A1 table are the two per-seed effects (seed 0, seed 1), not confidence intervals; a 2-seed screen computes none.</li><li><strong>A1 at equal wall-clock</strong> (in-training eval loss, SQ338 method): every winner still beats E27. A1g -6.6% (equal steps -8.9%), A1e -5.2%, A1a -3.0%, A1h -2.5%. A2 keeps the 6x2 shape.</li><li><strong>Data provenance (12:04 review):</strong> every A1/A2 box verifies v2 against the committed manifest's sha256 values before training. New side quests: SQ367 (atomic local dataset builds) and SQ368 (platform-tagged test pins).</li><li><strong>A2 wave setup:</strong></li><li>Six of 8 RTX 5090s are training; two are still being set up.</li><li>On box 2 at f85ada5: <code>tests/test_model.py</code> 12/12 and <code>tests/test_assembly.py</code> 9/9 pass on the GPU.</li><li><code>tests.test_moe</code> fails 15/15 on the x86-64 box. These are last-bit differences in pins recorded on the ARM64 host (CPU RNG and float reductions differ across architectures), not regressions; it passes 15/15 on ARM64 with the current code. Fix: SQ368.</li><li>A wave-2 driver bug was found and fixed before any job ran: <code>drive.sh</code> still wrote into the A1 folder, so boxes 2 and 4 got their A2 job lists from copies.</li><li><strong>Side-quest worker:</strong></li><li>SQ366 (per-doc NLL storage) and SQ341/SQ348 are done: the 200M loop cells are best at their trained r = 4 (r = 1 about 8% worse, r = 12 about 5% worse).</li><li>These results get integrated when the worker hands back.</li></ul>"
