   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 08:37 (Haiku) and quick reviews 08:34 (statistician) and 08:39 (ML theorist), triaged.</strong> Three of their ideas could be answered from runs already on disk, so they were run at once (descriptive, not registered):</p><p>| Check | Result | |---|---| | SQ336, leave-one-seed-out on the 200M I | no sign flip; per-seed I = +8.83%, +3.94%, +5.86% | | SQ337, I along training (in-training eval loss, not clean80) | <strong>-4.0% at step 250, 0 near ~107M tokens, +4.5% at the last eval</strong>: one rising trajectory, not a transient | | SQ338, equal wall-clock | the GDN cell takes 1.62x the dense time; its -3.4% per FLOP becomes <strong>+8.2% worse</strong> at equal wall-clock |</p><ul><li><strong>Corrections:</strong></li><li>The F2 devlog's \"the reversal is not an LR artifact\" overstated H2'. Cells 000 and 100 ran only at 3e-3 at 200M, so an LR confound remains open (SQ342; C202 limitation added).</li><li>The I figures are log-points (+6.21 log-points = +6.4% as a ratio).</li><li>The README now says C202 is PARTIAL, and that GDN's lead holds per FLOP only.</li><li><strong>Noted:</strong> looping halves the unique parameters at matched block applications (12.3M vs 27.9M), so the loops factor is also a unique-params factor (consistent with C197).</li><li><strong>New side quests:</strong></li><li>CPU: SQ339 (split the ternary cost into weights vs int8 activations, post hoc), SQ340 (fp32 reference scoring of cells 000, 100 and 111), SQ341 (loop-count curve on the loop cells). The 200M checkpoints are local.</li><li>GPU, needing a budget approval: SQ342 (200M LR completion), SQ343 (loop placement by block kind).</li><li>Merged: decay-only cell 111 into SQ235; per-name init generators into SQ332.</li><li>Rejected: A5 (per-cell LR at 20M), superseded by SQ342 at 200M; A8 (identifier renaming), covered by SQ194.</li><li><strong>Fleet:</strong> 0 instances; GPU budget spent.</li></ul>"
