   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 03:08 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ330:</strong> the GDN memory horizon, from learned decay half-lives (CPU). If most heads forget within 256 tokens, the long-memory reading of C18/C43 needs qualifying.</li><li><strong>SQ331:</strong> dynamic evaluation (per-document online adaptation), E1 vs E10.</li><li><strong>SQ332:</strong> an init-seed × data-seed variance split at d = 256. It needs a <code>--data-seed</code> option, because one seed drives both today.</li><li><strong>SQ333:</strong> an exploratory pairwise reading of C201 from the existing 2-ingredient cells.</li><li><strong>SQ334:</strong> a binding probe at distance.</li><li><strong>SQ222</strong> (fp32 vs bf16 recurrence) is promoted, since C197/C201 have no precision check.</li><li><strong>Flags answered:</strong></li><li>C201's 5-cell estimand is the registered design.</li><li>The log scale is the registered metric; a raw-scale I of about −4.2% is a sensitivity number, not the test.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 03:09 (newcomer):</strong> the README quick start now opens with a <strong>no-download, no-GPU first check</strong> (<code>tests.test_options</code> + <code>tests.test_moe</code> on CPU: 28 tests, about 10 s). It also adds a \"start reading here\" pointer to the three defining results:</p><ul><li>C5: no detected hybrid advantage over a tuned Llama;</li><li>C197: unique parameters beat loops at matched FLOPs;</li><li>C201: the fusion penalties overlap.</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet:</strong> E60's 200M runs are on their last seeds. The pull-and-destroy watcher takes each box down when it is idle.</p>"
