   "title": "Outside review 02:37: init-matched F2 check (SQ326), context-truncation intervention (SQ327); data-order pairing confirmed by code read",
   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 02:37 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ326, init-matched factorial sensitivity:</strong> accepted. The gogeta init costs 6-block attention about 3.5% (SQ200) but helps the 14-block hybrid about 7% (SQ308). F2's cells use the default gogeta init, so its main effects may be init-dependent. To be registered before running.</li><li><strong>SQ327:</strong> causal context truncation at eval (1024 → 512 → 256 visible tokens) on the 7+7 checkpoints. It is an intervention test of GDN state beyond the SWA window.</li><li><strong>SQ328:</strong> LR-column robustness of the F2 interaction, descriptive (n = 1 per column).</li><li><strong>SQ329:</strong> an eval-time re-injection gain sweep on E2, testing the over-looping failure (C7).</li><li><strong>Merges:</strong> the continuous overlap regression goes into SQ323, and SQ321 is a duplicate of SQ215.</li><li><strong>Rejected, the data-order pairing doubt:</strong> <code>TokenData</code> draws batches from its own generator seeded only by the train seed (<code>gogeta/train.py:61</code>). Same-seed arms therefore see identical batches, and the paired CIs are paired.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 02:35 (code-model practitioner):</strong></p><ul><li>SQ325: an import-context ablation on source-disjoint files.</li><li>Q14 (the standard code benchmarks) stays human-gated, because it needs dataset downloads and eval installs (AGENTS §0a).</li></ul><p><strong>E60 first GPU runs:</strong> the LR grid is running on w4-6.</p><ul><li>E60a's in-training val loss at 20M: 0.991 / <strong>0.979</strong> / 1.013 at lr 3e-3 / 6e-3 / 1.2e-2.</li><li>E60b: 0.994 / <strong>0.980</strong> / 1.033.</li><li>The registered choice uses clean80 after scoring.</li><li>MoE runs cost about 0.55 min per 20M run in steady state (the first run, 0.81 min, included compile).</li></ul>"
