   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Code-MoE FFN for E60</strong> (subagent, Opus; the main agent re-ran every suite):</p><ul><li><strong><code>gogeta/moe.py</code>:</strong> a dropless top-k MoE FFN with SwiGLU experts.</li><li>Routing is softmax top-k with renormalised gates, depends only on the current token, and has no capacity dropping and no expert-choice routing.</li><li>It adds a Switch balance loss and a router z-loss, with an optional frozen router.</li><li>The <code>gather</code> dispatch computes only the active experts; the <code>dense</code> dispatch is an option.</li><li><strong>Off by default:</strong> new <code>ModelConfig</code> fields <code>moe_*</code> (and mirrored in <code>gogeta/hf.py</code>), with <code>moe_experts = 0</code> meaning dense. With them off, models are <strong>bit-identical</strong>, pinned in <code>tests/test_moe.py</code> against values captured on the unmodified code. For E0/E1/E2/E3/E9/E11 it pins:</li><li>the initial state_dict sha256;</li><li>the RNG state after construction;</li><li><code>to_dict</code> and <code>param_counts</code>;</li><li>FLOPs as float hex;</li><li>the first 3 AdamW losses for E0/E1/E2.</li><li><strong><code>train.py</code>:</strong> the aux loss is added to the backward pass only for MoE models. Reported and val losses stay LM-only, and <code>moe/*</code> stats are logged.</li><li><strong>Tests, re-run by the main agent</strong> (<code>experiments/checks/results/test-runs/2026-11-23-C100-C80.txt</code>):</li><li><code>tests.test_options</code> + <code>tests.test_moe</code>: 28 OK, 1 skipped (needs a GPU);</li><li><code>post_training.test_hf</code>: 10/10;</li><li><code>evals.test_wiring</code>: 6/6.</li><li>Causality holds (perturbing future tokens leaves past logits within 1e-6).</li><li>Gather equals dense dispatch to 1e-5.</li><li><strong>E60 configs</strong> (<code>experiments/staged-configs/e60/</code>):</li></ul><p>| Arm | What it is | Non-embedding params | FLOPs vs E1 | |---|---|---|---| | E60a | 4 × 512 top-2 MoE | 18.2M total, 11.1M active | 1.00× | | E60b | E60a with a frozen router, balance/z-loss off | as E60a | 1.00× | | E60c | dense SwiGLU 2048, total-param matched | 18.2M | 1.47× |</p><ul><li><strong>Not yet measured:</strong> GPU throughput, and inductor compile of the gather path (it graph-breaks; the dense dispatch is the fallback).</li></ul><p><strong>E60 stage 1 registered</strong> (<code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>):</p><ul><li><strong>LR:</strong> a G3 grid at 20M (9 runs), then 3 arms × 6 seeds at 200M.</li><li><strong>Predictions:</strong></li><li><strong>M1:</strong> E60a − E1 = −1.8%;</li><li><strong>M2:</strong> E60c − E1 = −3.0%;</li><li><strong>M3:</strong> |E60a − E60b| ≤ 0.8%.</li><li><strong>Decisions:</strong> D1–D3 as in the design.</li><li><strong>Cost:</strong> about 2.5 GPU-h, about $1.5, which fits the remaining budget.</li><li>E60 is ungated by SQ282 and SQ238.</li></ul><p><strong>Outside review 02:09 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Accepted:</strong></li><li>SQ320: position-in-window loss split;</li><li>SQ321: a long causal conv mixer vs GDN;</li><li>SQ322: a one-rule TOST symmetry pass, a fair hit, because C197's \"unique params\" lever rests on SQ282's registered tie rule, not an equivalence test;</li><li>SQ323: clean-threshold sensitivity;</li><li>SQ324: a horizon replot.</li><li><strong>Rejected:</strong> a ternary width sweep, already covered by the F2 ternary factor, E3 and SQ290.</li></ul>"
