   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>SQ283, C197's seed replication</strong> (registered R1/R2; 200M tokens, lr 6e-3, seeds 0–3):</p><p>| Model | Mean clean80 bpc | vs E32 | |---|---|---| | E32 (14 unshared blocks) | <strong>0.2488</strong> | | | E2 (looped) | 0.2834 | E32 is <strong>12.2%</strong> better (paired CI [−13.1%, −11.3%], R1 PASS) | | E1 (7 seeds) | 0.2679 | E32 is <strong>7.15%</strong> better (Welch CI [−7.60%, −6.71%], R2 PASS) |</p><ul><li><strong>C197 is upgraded from PARTIAL to VERIFIED.</strong></li><li><strong>Caveats:</strong> the deep stack needs its depth-scaled init (SQ308), and the 200M arms all ran at 6e-3. At 20M, E32 is flat between 3e-3 and 6e-3.</li></ul><p><strong>SQ282, depth vs width with fair LRs</strong> (registered W1/W2; 20M tokens, 2 seeds, lr {3e-3, 6e-3, 1.2e-2}):</p><ul><li><strong>Best LRs:</strong> E32 3e-3 (0.4371), E34 3e-3 (<strong>0.4331</strong>), E2 6e-3 (0.4919).</li><li><strong>W1 FAIL:</strong> at their best LRs, the wide 5-block E34 <em>ties</em> the deep E32 (E32 is +0.93%, within 2 seed sd of 1.7%).</li><li>The v0.4.84 \"E34 is 14% worse\" was a learning-rate artifact: E34 is very LR-sensitive (+26% at 1.2e-2).</li><li>By the registered rule, <strong>C197's lever is unique parameters at matched FLOPs, not distinct depth.</strong></li><li><strong>W2 PASS:</strong> E34 beats the looped E2 by 12%.</li><li><strong>Consequence:</strong> E60 (Code-MoE, which adds width-like capacity) regains its prior. Its gates (SQ282 and SQ238) are both now closed.</li><li><strong>README:</strong> the scale sentence is corrected.</li></ul><p><strong>SQ238, the dedup-only control</strong> (registered D1–D3; 200M, E1, lr 6e-3, 4 seeds):</p><p>| Corpus | Mean clean80 bpc | |---|---| | code-py-v1sub (no dedup, v2's doc count) | 0.2663 | | code-py-v2 (deduplicated) | 0.2620 | | code-py-v1 (full) | 0.2679 |</p><ul><li><strong>Dedup effect</strong> D = <strong>+1.62%</strong>, paired CI [+0.92%, +2.31%], all 4 seeds positive. <strong>D1 PASS.</strong></li><li><strong>Coverage/size effect</strong> S = +0.64%. <strong>D2 PASS.</strong></li><li><strong>D3:</strong> D + S = 2.27%, against the H5 gap of 3.08% (single seed).</li><li><strong>Rule:</strong> the A3 v2 results stand as \"with dedup\".</li><li><strong>New claim C200, VERIFIED</strong> (one architecture and one LR, noted as limitations).</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>w4-3 sat idle about 65 min</strong> (00:55–02:00 EST) after SQ238 arm B. Its JOBS DONE line was lost during the operator hold and the monitor restarts, as happened with w4-5. It now runs SQ263.</li><li>New practice (also saved as an agent memory): after any monitor gap, check every rented box directly.</li><li>SQ263 (24 runs at 200M, blinded) is running on four boxes.</li><li><strong>Spend:</strong> about $19 of the approved $30.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick reviews:</strong></p><ul><li>01:44 (reproducibility auditor): SQ319, filling the TBD claim scopes; 117 of 127 definitions have one.</li><li>01:49 (safety): SQ61 gains a descendant-cleanup gate.</li></ul>"
