   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 01:38 (Haiku), triaged by the main agent:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ315: document-masked packing in training.</strong> Accepted (I1).</li><li>Training samples flat windows from an <code>&lt;|eos|&gt;</code>-separated stream with no attention mask or GDN state reset (<code>TokenData.batch()</code>; confirmed by reading the code).</li><li>Full attention, SWA and GDN use cross-document context differently, so the E1–E10 gap and C193's length effect may partly be packing.</li><li>SQ227 only changes scoring; this changes training.</li><li><strong>SQ316: locality-prior control.</strong> Accepted (I3): a sliding-window (256) Llama E10 at d = 256 against dense E10 and E1. If it matches E1, C198's small-width edge is the mask, not the linear mixer.</li><li><strong>SQ317:</strong> the base-loss cost of MTP auxiliary heads on E1, for goal 6's drafter (I4).</li><li><strong>SQ318:</strong> a per-token-class split of the E1–E10 gap on the 7+7 checkpoints (I5).</li><li><strong>SQ290</strong> gains a post-hoc ternary absmean arm (I6).</li><li><strong>Rejected:</strong> I2, a duplicate of SQ235 (the delta-rule ablation).</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 01:39 (newcomer):</strong> the guided-trace idea is rejected (the learn page and run forms already cover it), and the question \"what is the headline while F2 is blinded\" is answered in the triage footer.</p><p><strong>Fleet:</strong> F2 stage 2 is running on four boxes (scores blinded) and SQ238 arm B is on w4-3.</p>"
