   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>F2 blinded variance re-estimation</strong> (registered in the wave-5 amendment). This is recorded <strong>before</strong> stage 2 dispatches.</p><ul><li><strong>Estimator:</strong> <code>experiments/design/f2_blinded_sigma.py</code>, committed in v0.4.89 before it was run. Output is in <code>experiments/checks/results/f2_blinded_sigma.json</code>.</li><li><strong>Stage 1:</strong> 135 runs, 27 seeds × 5 cells, including the pilot's seeds 0–2.</li><li><strong>Sigma:</strong> seed-blocked log-sd <strong>0.00873</strong> (residual df 104); unblocked 0.00945.</li><li><strong>Registered rule:</strong> N_final = min(246, ⌈235·(σ_blocked/0.009)²⌉) = <strong>221</strong>.</li><li><strong>Allocation:</strong> the registered shape (E20 twice the others) gives E20 = 74 and the other cells 37 each. <strong>Stage 2 = 87 runs</strong>: E20 seeds 27–73, the other cells seeds 27–36, at the registered LRs.</li><li><strong>Nothing else was computed or looked at:</strong> no cell means, contrasts or interaction estimates. The display-blinding disclosure is in v0.4.89, and more is below.</li><li><strong>Design note, found now:</strong> under the seed-blocked primary model, a seed run by only one cell adds no information about the cell contrasts. So E20's seeds 37–73 inform only the unblocked sensitivity analysis and E20's own variance.</li><li>The registered allocation is followed unchanged; changing it after seeing stage-1 sigma would itself be a deviation.</li><li>The primary analysis's effective N for contrasts is the 37 seeds shared by all five cells.</li><li>The analysis must report this alongside the power.</li><li><strong>More blinding exposure</strong> (quick review 01:10, SQ313):</li><li><strong>67 F2 stage-1 per-run score files were committed and pushed in v0.4.88</strong>, so they are publicly readable;</li><li>they are no longer copied into the repo until this step;</li><li>review agents are told not to compute per-cell F2 results.</li></ul><p><strong>code-py-v1sub (SQ238's control data) is verified:</strong></p><ul><li>two boxes, w4-1 and w4-5, built it independently in 43 s and 37 s, with byte-identical output (train.bin sha256 <code>7e0f15f1…</code>);</li><li>698,714 docs, 196.5M tokens;</li><li>manifest: <code>experiments/data_integrity/dataset-v1sub.manifest.json</code>;</li><li>details in <code>notes/data-v2.md</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>w4-5 is destroyed</strong> (2.78 h, about $1.65). It sat idle for about 40 min after its last batch: its JOBS DONE event was lost while the operator hold and monitor restarts were in progress. Its inference outputs (knockout, ensemble, docnll) were pulled first.</li><li>Five boxes remain.</li><li><strong>Queue reconciled:</strong> Q7/Q8 are marked done; they ran on the N1X and are superseded by the 7-seed 5090 arms.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick reviews:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>01:10 and 01:24 (safety):</strong> SQ61 now requires a fail-closed GRPO reward path that refuses to score when network or filesystem isolation is missing (C83). SQ313 is the blinding redaction check.</li><li><strong>01:18 (cheapest-experiment hunter):</strong> the Q8 preflight idea is rejected, since Q8 was a stale entry and the launcher already runs a preflight.</li></ul>"
