   "date": "2026-11-23",
   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 01:07 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Idea A (accepted, registered as SQ308):</strong> the default \"gogeta\" init scales residual outputs by 0.02/√(2·depth) (<code>gogeta/model.py</code>, <code>_init_weights</code>).</li><li>That gives std 0.0058 for 6-block E1 and 0.0038 for 14-block E32.</li><li>So C197's \"14 unshared blocks beat E1 by 7%\" is also an init comparison, and C199 shows init can move all-attention stacks by 3.5–3.8%.</li><li><strong>SQ308 design:</strong> E1 and E32 at 20M tokens × {gogeta, flat} × seeds 0–2, 12 runs. Configs are sha-bound; <code>staged-configs/sq308/e32_flat.json</code> is new.</li><li><strong>G1:</strong> the E32 init effect is within ±1%.</li><li><strong>G2:</strong> E32 beats E1 by ≥ 3% under both inits.</li><li><strong>Rule:</strong> a flat-init gap within ±1% means C197's lever is an init artifact.</li><li><strong>Also accepted:</strong></li><li>SQ309: length-bucketed sampling, testing whether C193's long-document deficit is data exposure;</li><li>SQ310: an equal wall-clock replot from existing logs (CPU);</li><li>SQ311: E32 on the out-of-corpus length bins;</li><li>SQ312: zero-init residual branches.</li><li><strong>README (the review's flag, AGENTS §0 wording lag):</strong> the width sentences now say:</li><li>\"no difference detected\" at d = 512, instead of \"ties\";</li><li>E1 is 1.2–1.7% better at d = 256 (exploratory, with SQ307 running);</li><li>the init result is C199 PARTIAL, and SQ308 checks the C197 init confound.</li></ul>"
