   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 23:39 (Haiku), triaged.</strong> Fact-checked against <code>experiments/checks/results/sq243_sq241.json</code>.</p><ul><li><strong>C198's d = 256 endpoint is weak:</strong></li><li>E10's four seeds have sd 0.0021, against 0.0003 for E1 (7×).</li><li>E1 does beat E10 on all four seeds, so the review's \"driven by three seeds\" is an overstatement; but the size of the gap rests on E10's noise.</li><li>The LRs were never re-tuned per width.</li><li>E1 also uses FusionDance's init and E10 uses HF's. SQ200, running now, measures that confound at d = 384.</li><li><strong>SQ301 registered and queued</strong> (<code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>): an LR-fair re-test at d = 256.</li><li>E1 and E10 at lr {3e-3, 6e-3, 1.2e-2} × seeds 0–1, reusing the existing cells: 8 new runs.</li><li><strong>W1:</strong> E10's best LR is ≥ 6e-3.</li><li><strong>W2:</strong> the best-vs-best gap lies in [−1.0%, +0.25%].</li><li><strong>Rule:</strong> a gap within ±0.5% refutes C198.</li><li><strong>README:</strong> the \"scale looks like the lever\" sentence now carries the E34 caveat from v0.4.84 (a wide 5-block model at E32's parameters and FLOPs is 14% worse, so the lever may be distinct depth).</li><li><strong>New side quests:</strong></li><li>SQ302: LR transfer across width (muP-style), which feeds the final-model LR;</li><li>SQ303: grow unique depth onto a trained E1;</li><li>SQ304: per-seed loss-curve diagnosis.</li><li><strong>Rejected:</strong> EMA as a power tool (SQ217 covers EMA, and a headline-metric change needs its own registration), and an E32/E2 redundancy probe (covered by SQ248 and SQ265).</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 23:39 (code-model practitioner, Codex):</strong></p><ul><li>SQ300, a patch-repair pilot: a capability gate for the final model, gated on <code>generate()</code>.</li><li>The identifier reuse-distance idea is merged into SQ209.</li><li>The whitespace probe is rejected as a duplicate of SQ194.</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet:</strong></p><ul><li>The SQ238 dedup-control dataset <code>code-py-v1sub</code> is built on w4-1: 698,714 docs, 196.5M tokens, 179,069 v1-val-linked docs excluded, train.bin sha256 <code>7e0f15f1...</code>, built in 43 s.</li><li>Its 4 seeds are training.</li><li>Its manifest is committed only after a second box reproduces it byte for byte.</li><li>136 jobs are queued (wave 6 remainder, SQ238 arm B, F2 stage 1).</li></ul>"
