   "version": "v0.4.85",
   "title": "Goal 6: a final model on a 24 GB RTX 3090/4090 (plan, E61); SQ243 width effect (C198); SQ241; byte LR 3e-3; corpus v3 plan",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>New goal 6 (the human's request): ship the final model on a gaming GPU.</strong> End the experiments with one model that runs batch-1 inference with a KV/state cache and lossless speculative decoding on a single 24 GB RTX 3090 or 4090. Added to the goals in DEVLOG and README; goal 5 now says the experiments run locally <em>or on cheap rented GPUs</em>.</p><ul><li><strong>Plan:</strong> <code>notes/final-model-plan.md</code> (planning subagent; the main agent re-derived the headline numbers).</li><li><strong>What binds is training money and unique tokens, not VRAM:</strong></li><li>24 GB holds about 9B params in bf16;</li><li>every size we can afford fits with room for more than 1M tokens of cache;</li><li>training costs about $2.15 per 1e18 FLOPs on a 5090 (computed from E1's measured 743k tok/s at $0.523/h, which assumes the 14M-scale efficiency carries over; SQ297 measures it).</li><li><strong>Primary target G-1B:</strong></li><li>about 1.23B params: 24 blocks in E1's pattern (12 GDN, 8 SWA, 4 full attention), d = 2048, GQA with 4 KV heads;</li><li>about 24–32B tokens, about $500–650 all-in;</li><li>estimated (not measured) decode on a 3090: about 300 tok/s in bf16 and about 450–600 in int8;</li><li>cache: 8 KiB per token, so about 1 GB at 128k context.</li><li><strong>Stretch G-3B:</strong> about $2.8k. It needs Stack v3 data and sharded training, and is worth it only if the scaling fit predicts at least 5% better than G-1B.</li><li><strong>Speculative decoding:</strong> a separate drafter or MTP heads are estimated at 1.5–2.9×. Self-speculation by fewer loops comes to about 1.3–1.6×.</li><li><code>gogeta/model.py</code> checks out: nothing in a loop pass depends on the total r, so the draft's pass caches can be reused.</li><li>None of these acceptance rates has been measured.</li><li><strong>Gated, not assumed:</strong> loops, ternary, MoE and the spec-decode scheme each enter the final model only if their gates pass. Milestones run from M1 (inference stack plus a 3090/4090 rental smoke test, under $2) to M4 (the final train). <strong>M4 needs the human's approval.</strong></li><li><strong>Registered:</strong> E61 \"Final model\" (planned) in <code>experiments/experiments.json</code>, and side quests SQ285–SQ298: sm_86/sm_89 kernels, KV/SWA cache with <code>generate()</code>, self-spec cache reuse, decode benchmark, memory envelope, int8/int4 PTQ, scaling-law fit, repeat-epoch penalty, GQA, long context, the 4090 L2 ternary core, drafter/MTP acceptance.</li><li><strong>Open for the human:</strong> AGENTS §2 reserves v1.0.0 for the full fusion. If loops or ternary fail their gates, the final model is hybrid-only. Should it still be 1.0.0?</li></ul><p><strong>SQ243 two-size check</strong> (16 runs on RTX 5090s, clean80 bpc, E1 at lr 6e-3 and E10 at 3e-3 at every width; <code>experiments/checks/results/sq243_sq241.json</code>):</p><p>| Width | E1 − E10 | Paired 95% CI | Prediction | |---|---|---|---| | d = 512 | +0.05% | [−0.33%, +0.44%] | S1 PASS (tie) | | d = 384 | +0.08% | (Phase 2b, 7 seeds) | | | d = 256 | <strong>−1.24%</strong> | [−2.24%, −0.25%] | <strong>S2 FAIL</strong> (E1 better) |</p><ul><li><strong>S3:</strong> a scaling effect is called at the d = 256 end point.</li><li><strong>Read:</strong> E1's linear mixers help only at the smallest width and the edge is gone by d = 384.</li><li><strong>But the LRs were not re-tuned per width</strong> (a registered limitation). Small models often want higher LRs, so E10 at 3e-3 may be under-tuned at d = 256.</li><li><strong>New claim C198, PARTIAL</strong> [exploratory: LRs not re-tuned per width]. Its refutation test is a per-width LR sweep.</li></ul><p><strong>SQ241 param-matched E1</strong> (mlp_hidden 952, 10.62M non-embedding params, 4 seeds):</p><ul><li><strong>vs E10:</strong> +0.61%. P1 PASS (within ±1%).</li><li><strong>vs full E1:</strong> +0.53%. P2 FAIL, by 0.03 points over the 0.5% bound (paired CI [+0.05%, +1.21%]).</li><li><strong>So</strong> part of E1's tie with E10 rests on its 0.5M extra MLP params. This is added to C5 as evidence (event 11).</li></ul><p><strong>Byte Quest:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ188 LR sweep, e13b at 20M bytes</strong> (val loss, nats/byte):</li><li>lr 1.5e-3: 2.757 (the registered extension point);</li><li>lr 3e-3: <strong>2.712</strong>;</li><li>lr 6e-3: 2.967;</li><li>lr 1.2e-2: 2.869.</li><li>L1 (minimum at 6e-3 or above) and L2 (a flat basin) are both <strong>refuted</strong>. The registered rule puts every E13 arm at <strong>3e-3</strong>.</li><li>These runs are short (153 steps), and the 6e-3 &gt; 1.2e-2 ordering suggests noise at this length.</li><li><strong>E15b crashed and is fixed:</strong></li><li><code>Triton Error [CUDA]: invalid argument</code> in fla's chunk GDN kernel;</li><li>cause: the parallel-refine decoder runs GDN over 32 × 1,025 patch groups × 3 heads, more than 65,535 rows on one CUDA grid axis;</li><li>fix: <code>GatedDeltaNet._run_kernel</code> splits the batch, which is exact because sequences are independent (WIP <code>c064d29</code>; <code>test_byte_model</code> 24/24);</li><li>the retry benches at 276k tok/s, 10.25 GB.</li><li><strong>SQ189 benches</strong> (tok/s and peak memory):</li><li>E13b: 82.1k, 7.41 GB;</li><li>E14b: 110k, 9.39 GB;</li><li>E14c: 700k, 13.4 GB;</li><li>E13a: 368k, 10.7 GB.</li><li><strong>Now running:</strong> the E13 patch-size sweep at 3e-3 plus E13b at 200M.</li></ul><p><strong>Corpus v3 research (the human's request):</strong> research agent, <code>notes/research-corpus-v3.md</code>.</p><ul><li><strong>Primary:</strong> The Stack v3 train split (rev <code>159792e7</code>).</li><li>ODC-By, not gated;</li><li>repo-level rows, so we can finally split at repo level;</li><li>Python is about 5% of bytes, so 2.5B tokens means about 80–105 GB of shards.</li><li><strong>Fallback:</strong> codeparrot-clean (12.8 GB, about 8B permissive tokens).</li><li><strong>Downloads are human-only and not done.</strong> SQ276 (a metadata-only shard census, a few GB) comes first.</li><li><strong>SQ276–SQ281 added</strong> to the side quests.</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet:</strong></p><ul><li>Wave 6 is running on 5 boxes: the SQ200 init 2×2 and the Inkling loop-variant runs, with SQ282 started.</li><li>w4-1 is on Byte Quest.</li><li>The inference batch finished: the docnll scorer matches the reference scorer within 1e-6 on every checkpoint it scored (max diff seen 3.6e-7). Analysis is pending.</li><li><strong>Early SQ200 signal</strong> (seed 0/2, analysis pending): E0 with flat init 0.5889/0.5858 vs gogeta init 0.6076/0.6068 in-training val, which points to the init handicap.</li></ul>"
