   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 00:10 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>C197 is confounded.</strong> E34 (E9's 5-block layout widened to d=576) has about the same unique params and FLOPs as E32, yet scores <strong>0.2834 vs 0.2486, 14% worse</strong>. So \"unique params at matched FLOPs\" is not sufficient: at matched params and FLOPs, <em>distinct depth</em> beat width here. Both ran at untuned LRs, n=1.</li><li><strong>Ledger:</strong> C197 gets a limitation (event 4); it stays PARTIAL [exploratory n=1].</li><li><strong>New items, registered and queued:</strong></li><li><strong>SQ282:</strong> LR-fair depth vs width. E32, E34 and E2 × 3 LRs × 2 seeds at 20M.</li><li><strong>SQ283:</strong> C197 seed replication. E32 and E2 at 200M, seeds 1–3.</li><li><strong>SQ284:</strong> per-pass unique low-rank adapters in the shared loop. Accepted, needs a model option.</li><li><strong>Queue reordered:</strong> wave 6, then SQ282/SQ283, then SQ263 (the 200M factorial gate), then F2.</li><li><strong>E60 (Code-MoE) is gated on SQ282 and SQ238,</strong> because its prior assumes width-like capacity helps.</li></ul><p><strong>Inkling 2 Mini research (the human's request):</strong> research agent, <code>notes/research-inkling2-mini.md</code>, cited sources; not every fact re-verified by the main agent.</p><ul><li><strong>Model:</strong> Thinking Machines Lab, released 2026-11-20. A 26.4B/3.4B-active MoE whose layers 6–17 run 3× with shared weights (layers 0–5 and 18–23 run once).</li><li><strong>The loop slightly loses on training compute</strong> (7.5%) but wins on parameters and inference.</li><li><strong>Ingredients we lack:</strong></li><li>a closed-gate restart, so the looped net starts out <em>exactly</em> its unlooped twin;</li><li>no residual carry between passes;</li><li>a fixed r = 3 (we sample U{1..7});</li><li>thick outer layers (a quarter of the layers on each side; ours is 1/3/1);</li><li>gated messages plus attention residuals.</li><li><strong>SQ266–SQ273 added.</strong> The config-only SQ266 (fixed-r sweep) and SQ271 (thick outer layers) are registered as wave 6 part 3: 21 runs, predictions K1–K4.</li><li><strong>Correction:</strong> <code>notes/research-looped.md</code>'s \"Inkling 2 is not looped\" is true only for Inkling 2 <em>Small</em>.</li><li>3 papers were listed in <code>refs/fetch_refs.py</code> and <strong>not downloaded</strong> (human-only).</li></ul><p><strong>Wave 4 so far:</strong></p><ul><li>SQ243 at d = 512: E1 0.5262–0.5295 vs E10 0.5265–0.5268 in-training val.</li><li>SQ241 param-matched E1: 0.5875–0.5881. Clean80 scoring is pending.</li><li>Inference (SQ248 knockouts) is running.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick reviews:</strong> 23:05 (SQ275, bound the SWA mask cache) and 23:09 (rejected as covered by C190/K1/SQ244). A research agent is searching for a better code corpus (the human's request).</p>"
