   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>code-py-v2 builder</strong> (<code>experiments/data_integrity/build_v2.py</code>, <code>notes/data-v2.md</code>; subagent, tests re-run by the main agent: 7/7 pass).</p><ul><li><strong>Families:</strong> 64-perm MinHash over token 8-grams, est. Jaccard ≥ 0.5, single linkage over train and val.</li><li><strong>Train</strong> keeps one doc per family.</li><li><strong>Val</strong> is redrawn: the v1 val docs first, then seeded train singletons, each with under 30% of its 13-grams in train. Every val doc's whole family leaves train, and so does any train doc sharing a rare def/class name with a val doc (one hop).</li><li><strong>Checks:</strong> the build asserts the final overlap and family audit.</li><li><strong>Determinism:</strong> a 1-worker build is byte-identical to a 3-worker build.</li><li><strong>Status:</strong> it unblocks most of A3 (E20–E27, E35, E36, E40–E53). The full build runs next on a rented 5090's CPU, twice on two boxes, to prove the manifests match. v2 val numbers are not comparable with v1 val (it is redrawn).</li></ul><p><strong>CPU analyses (subagent; numbers spot-checked by the main agent):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ225, source mix:</strong></li><li>The val/train config mix matches (algorithmic_corpus 63.9% vs 62.9%, chi2 1.70).</li><li>The K9 near-duplicate overlap is concentrated by source: 52.3% of algorithmic val docs vs 22.9% of synthetic (+29.3 pts, CI 26.6–32.2). So clean-val results lean toward synthetic_code_snippet.</li><li><strong>C131:</strong> limitation added.</li><li><strong>SQ228, repetition vs length</strong> (330 out-of-corpus files, package-clustered bootstrap):</li><li>8-gram repeat share correlates 0.48 with log length.</li><li>Jointly, it absorbs about 27% of the length coefficient (1.55 → 1.13 per SD). Length survives.</li><li><strong>C193:</strong> evidence added, no status change (exploratory).</li><li><strong>SQ233, C1/C3:</strong></li><li>C3's attention and SWA causality checks were re-run on CPU and pass (past-token diff 0.0).</li><li>C1 and the GDN/looped parts of C3 need fla's Triton GPU kernels. Their JSON stores the recorded values, labelled <code>recorded</code>.</li><li>Next: a GPU re-run on a rented 5090.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 21:26 (skeptical peer reviewer):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Accepted:</strong> queue reconciliation at the end of each fleet wave.</li><li><strong>Rejected:</strong> E1 vs E10 at matched FLOPs, because the token-matched comparison is already conservative against E1 (91.0M vs 96.8M FLOPs/token) and E31 covers the dense side.</li></ul><p><strong>PREDICTIONS erratum:</strong> the wave-2 heading's \"~21:45\" was an estimate. It was actually written at about 21:22, still before dispatch.</p>"
