   "html": "<p><strong>Expenses are now tracked</strong> (the human: \"lets track our expenses\").</p><ul><li><strong>Ledger:</strong> <code>experiments/expenses.json</code>, append-only: credit purchases, per-rental compute (estimated), and reconciliations against the provider's own numbers. Cockpit access: <code>bash cockpit/cockpit.sh --expenses [reconcile]</code>, MCP <code>gogeta_expenses</code> and <code>gogeta_expenses_reconcile</code> (80/80 tests).</li><li><strong>Public-repo rule:</strong> amounts and purposes only. No card digits, receipt numbers or links, addresses or e-mails; the reconcile path keeps only the two numbers it needs.</li><li><strong>To date:</strong></li><li><strong>$100.00</strong> Vast.ai credit bought by the human (2026-11-22 16:54 PST);</li><li><strong>$0.4239</strong> compute actually charged, against $0.34 estimated across the 3090 and 5090 pilot boxes; the $0.08 gap is boot, storage and bandwidth time;</li><li><strong>$99.58</strong> credit left.</li><li>Auto-billing is off (credit-only), so Vast cannot charge the card on its own.</li></ul><p><strong>Outside review 21:10 (Haiku), triaged:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Critiques accepted:</strong></li><li>SQ214's \"w64 worse\" is not significant at n = 4 (erratum in its devlog), and the C193 limitation rests on the aggregate, not the &gt; 1,200-token bin.</li><li>E1 vs E10 mixes mixer and init (SQ234).</li><li><strong>At n = 3 the Phase 2b verdict sits at about 0.5 SE</strong>, so 7 seeds per arm are needed for a 0.3% effect.</li><li><strong>New queue items:</strong> SQ234 (E1 under E10's init), SQ235 (delta-rule ablation), SQ236 (membership gap), SQ237 (GDN-only length extrapolation).</li><li><strong>Quick reviews:</strong> 21:10 reproducibility auditor gave SQ232 (same-SKU replay floor) and SQ233 (machine-readable outputs for the VERIFIED C1/C3).</li></ul><p><strong>Fleet wave 1 registered before dispatch</strong> (<code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>). The human asked for \"several of the cheapest 5090s, max 8 concurrent\", running every experiment, CPU jobs included, and the N1X limited to light work after its 86.6 °C thermal kill.</p><ul><li><strong>Phase 2b-5090,</strong> an independent single-SKU replication: E10 and E1 at <strong>7 seeds each</strong>, E11 × 3, E9 and E2 × 1, all at 200M tokens, scored on clean80.</li><li>The N1X 3 + 3-seed E1-vs-E10 comparison stays the registered confirmatory Q12 test.</li><li>The two SKUs are never pooled.</li><li>Predictions R1–R3. The resolvable effect is stated up front: a half-width of about 0.0018 at n = 7, under an assumed sd.</li><li><strong>SQ232:</strong> same-SKU replay pairs for E10 and E1. Prediction P-R1: |Δ| ≤ 0.002.</li></ul>"
