   "html": "<p><strong>Outside review 20:40 (Haiku), triaged</strong> (<code>notes/reviews/2026-11-22-2040-review.md</code>, footer):</p><ul><li><strong>SQ226 (top pick, CPU): reset-matched scoring control.</strong> C193's &gt; 1,200-token reversal sits exactly where the scorer switches to chunked 1,024/512 windows, which restarts GDN state, so the \"length effect\" may be a scorer artifact.</li><li><strong>SQ227:</strong> document-boundary carry-over.</li><li><strong>SQ228:</strong> in-document repetition vs length as the covariate.</li><li><strong>SQ229:</strong> schedule robustness of the E1-vs-E10 order.</li><li><strong>Idea E adopted before any SQ214 run.</strong> The window sweep goes from 2 to <strong>4 seeds per arm</strong> as a pre-run amendment in <code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>, with W1–W3 unchanged and a scoring caveat pointing to SQ226.</li><li><strong>Rejected:</strong> moving the Phase 2b verdict to the frozen test split (a post-registration change of the confirmatory set is a forking path; it stays an extra check, SQ218).</li></ul><p><strong>Quick review 20:40 (ML theorist):</strong> SQ230 (a loop-pass representation probe on E2) is accepted.</p><p><strong>New rule, AGENTS §0h (the human, 2026-11-22: \"kill them unless we have no work queued up... if there is no more work pull down\"):</strong></p><ul><li>Rented GPUs live only while work is queued: rent just in time, size the fleet to the queue.</li><li>When a box's last job ends, pull its results and destroy it. A box idle for more than 10 min is destroyed.</li><li>Batch runs per box to amortise setup.</li><li>Status updates list every live box with its spend vs the $30 / 12 h budget.</li><li>Applied right away: the 3090 pilot (instance 62070434) was destroyed when its work was done, after about 40 min, roughly $0.15.</li></ul><p><strong>The setup is now clean end to end:</strong></p><ul><li><code>cockpit/remote/fetch_data.sh</code> rebuilt the whole <code>code-py-v1</code> dataset on a fresh RTX 5090 from the public Hugging Face source (2.79 GB in about 40 s on the box's link) in <strong>46 s</strong> of build time.</li><li>All four files match <code>experiments/data_integrity/dataset.manifest.json</code> byte for byte: <code>train.bin</code> <code>db61140a…</code>, <code>val.bin</code> <code>32e4b0ed…</code>, <code>docs_val.jsonl</code> <code>f821d119…</code>, <code>tokenizer.json</code> <code>0e75f39f…</code>. The builder is deterministic on a different machine.</li><li><code>bootstrap.sh</code> from scratch took 76 s on the 5090.</li><li>From rent to ready, nothing is uploaded from the operator's machine (the 3090 pilot spent 494 s uploading).</li><li><strong>Two fixes:</strong></li><li><code>python -P</code>, because <code>tools/queue.py</code> shadowed the stdlib <code>queue</code> that pyarrow imports;</li><li>an inline comment had swallowed the script's error handler.</li><li><strong>Live:</strong> RTX 5090 instance 62073471 ($0.523/hr) is running SQ220 part 2 (bridge) and the SQ214 sweep (12 runs plus clean-val scoring); results come in the next entry.</li></ul>"
