   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What:</strong> the first rented GPU run (SQ220, 1x RTX 3090 on Vast.ai, approved by the human: \"get 1 working first\", $30 / 12 h cap). Also the 20:05 claim-audit verifier's findings, three quick reviews, and the SQ214 window sweep registered for a rented RTX 5090.</p><p><strong>SQ220, the 3090 part</strong> (<code>experiments/devlogs/SQ220.md</code>):</p><ul><li><strong>Setup:</strong> the same commit (<code>9712842</code>, clean clone, <code>--require-clean</code>), the same sha256-verified data and the same software stack as the N1X, with K7's bridge runs at seed 0, lr 3e-3, 20M tokens.</li><li><strong>Loss transfers:</strong></li><li>E10: 1.0306 vs the N1X's 1.0286 (Δ +0.0020);</li><li>E1: 1.0078 vs 1.0071 (Δ +0.0007).</li></ul><p>Both are within the provisional ±0.004 reproduction tolerance (P1 passes, <code>STATISTICAL</code>). E1 &lt; E10 holds on both GPUs.</p><ul><li><strong>Speed (steady-state median tokens/s):</strong></li><li>E10: 272.5k vs 202.0k, <strong>1.35×</strong>;</li><li>E1: 254.5k vs 138.0k, <strong>1.84×</strong>.</li></ul><p>The registered 2–3× (P3) is a partial miss: at 13.8M params the runs look overhead-bound, not bandwidth-bound.</p><ul><li><strong>Whole-run throughput on a fresh box misleads:</strong> E1 was 0.94× because of the cold Triton/fla autotune cache, about 1 min of fixed cost per box.</li><li><strong>Incidents:</strong></li><li>the <code>pytorch/pytorch</code> image has no C compiler, so Inductor failed (fixed with apt build-essential);</li><li>the 525 MB dataset took 494 s over the operator's link.</li></ul><p><strong>Making the next rental quick (the human asked: \"make this easier for the next time\"):</strong></p><ul><li><code>cockpit/remote/bootstrap.sh</code>: a one-shot, idempotent box setup. It runs apt (compiler, git), uv, the pinned Python 3.12 venv (torch 2.14.1+cu130, triton 3.8.0, fla 0.6.0, plus transformers 5.24.0 and einops 0.8.2, which <code>requirements.txt</code> omits), the clone at the exact commit, and a <code>torch.compile</code> GPU smoke test. Verified on the 3090: a re-run takes 19 s and ends in <code>ENV OK</code>.</li><li><code>cockpit/remote/fetch_data.sh</code>: rebuilds the dataset on the box from the public Hugging Face source with the committed tokenizer, and verifies it file by file against <code>experiments/data_integrity/dataset.manifest.json</code>. A mismatch falls back to the sha256-checked upload and is never used for training. The live rebuild test was still running at commit time; its result goes in the next entry.</li><li>The cockpit's provider-pluggable fleet tooling (Vast first, MCP-driven, budget-guarded) is being built by a subagent and lands separately.</li></ul><p><strong>Claim audit 2005, checked by the main agent:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>C192 PARTIAL → REFUTED.</strong> The registered pooled criterion refutes it, and the earlier move to PARTIAL rested on a post-hoc length cut, which <code>notes/statistics-policy.md:49</code> says can never change a status. The length finding stays in C193.</li><li><strong>C71 is superseded by C194</strong>, the same KDA decode claim without the contrast with GDN that our own data contradicts.</li><li><strong>C16 UNVERIFIED → INCONCLUSIVE.</strong> K3 ran but its validity gate failed (an invalid control is INCONCLUSIVE per the ledger README).</li><li>Limitations were added to C193, C121, C125 and C93, and evidence pointers to C67, C68 and C69.</li><li>Three auditor verdicts were rejected after checking the PDFs (C30, C35, C76).</li></ul><p><strong>Quick reviews:</strong></p><ul><li>20:20 cheapest-experiment hunter: rejected.</li><li>20:24 statistician: SQ224, leave-one-seed-pair-out fragility.</li><li>20:32 data engineer: SQ225, source-config mix audit.</li><li>The 20:10 safety review (SQ223) is filed.</li></ul><p><strong>Registered (before any run):</strong></p><ul><li>SQ214 window sweep: E1 with SWA window 64/256/1024, seeds 0–1, 20M tokens, on one rented RTX 5090. It is exploratory, with clean-val bpc as the primary metric. Predictions W1–W3, configs hash-bound in <code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>.</li><li>SQ220 part 2 (5090 bridge): 5-P1 to 5-P3.</li></ul><p><strong>Docs refresh (hourly):</strong> README and sketch were updated with the C192/C193/C16 states and the Byte Quest registration facts. The refresh agent's \"no instance rented\" line was corrected by the main agent.</p>"
