   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong> (the human: \"update the uarch graphics and documentation in the gh pages site and the readme, byte level tokens are a thing now\"; a subagent built it, the main agent verified it):</p><ul><li><strong>README:</strong> a \"Byte Quest: bytes are a main quest now\" section, covering:</li><li>the new SVG diagram <code>docs/assets/byte-quest-c2f.svg</code>: byte encoder → patches → global stack → <strong>causal one-patch shift</strong> → byte refinement loop × r → 256-way head; transparent and mid-tone, for GitHub light and dark mode;</li><li>why bytes, the coarse-to-fine idea and its estimated cost;</li><li>the E12–E16 table linked to the cards;</li><li>the honest caveat (bytes trail BPE at our scale; the claims are about granularity and loops).</li></ul><p>Also from the newcomer review: the <strong>stale SQ99 sentence is replaced</strong> (\"no evidence of E1's in-corpus advantage out of corpus; CI −0.1%..+1.0%\"), and there's a <strong>\"Start here\" path</strong> with \"if the README and the ledger disagree, the ledger wins\".</p><ul><li><strong>Landing page:</strong> a <code>#bytes</code> section with the diagram, the E12–E16 table, and links to cards, devlogs and the 3D page.</li><li><strong>3D explorer:</strong> a <strong>\"C2F-byte (concept)\" model</strong> (key 8, <code>?model=c2f_byte</code>): byte cubes, encoder, patch tiles, E1's real global stack on patches, the shift lines, a raw-byte re-inject skip, a byte refinement ring with ghost pillars per extra pass, and the 256-way head. It has a <strong>P slider (2/4/8)</strong>, r limited to 1–4, 5 new legend rows and a \"design concept: estimates, not a trained model\" banner. The power-level readout reproduces the analysis table at P = 4 (95/108/135 M = 1.04/1.19/1.48× E1); P = 2/8 are labelled extrapolations.</li><li>The site build lists E12–E16 automatically (experiment pages E12–E16.html).</li><li>The Learn page is generated from <code>site-src/learn.md</code>, so the \"Bytes vs tokens\" explainer is the unapplied patch <code>notes/patches/site-bytes-learn.patch</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Verified by the main agent</strong> (browser pane):</p><ul><li><strong>labels stay at 22 → 22</strong> across full sweeps of every slider and the self-test;</li><li><code>__arch3dSelfTest(3)</code> passes;</li><li>a second run is perfectly flat (geometries 45 → 45, textures 3 → 3); the first-run +5 is a one-time cache fill;</li><li>no console errors;</li><li>the scene renders as designed (screenshot checked).</li></ul><p>The subagent reports 375 px width with no horizontal scroll.</p><p><strong>Not verified</strong>: the SVG on a pure white background; the 3D visuals at P = 2/8.</p>"
