   "version": "v0.4.66",
   "title": "SQ99 reversed: E1's advantage is length-dependent, not corpus-specific; outside review 20:07",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### SQ99 length re-analysis (from outside review 20:07, idea I1; CPU, saved per-doc NLL) The out-of-corpus docs average about 1,210 tokens vs about 300 in corpus (computed), so the reviewer suspected a length confound. <strong>Confirmed.</strong> E1-vs-E0 gap by doc length (package-clustered 95% CIs):</p><ul><li>0–300 tokens: <strong>−3.86%</strong> (−4.94..−2.60, 29 docs);</li><li>300–600: −2.39% (−3.39..−1.32, 52);</li><li>600–1,200: −0.56% (−1.13..+0.11, 96);</li><li><strong>&gt; 1,200: +1.09% (+0.48..+1.74, 153).</strong></li></ul><p><strong>On short out-of-corpus files E1's advantage matches its in-corpus size (−3.44%);</strong> the pooled null is driven by long files.</p><ul><li><strong>Reading:</strong> SQ99's \"does not transfer\" was mostly a <strong>length/long-context effect</strong>, not a corpus effect. E1 (1 attention, 2 SWA-256, 3 GDN) may fall behind E0 (6 full-attention layers) when context beyond a few hundred tokens matters. Length is confounded with file type, and this is exploratory (n=1).</li><li><strong>Ledger:</strong> new claim <strong>C193</strong> (the gap shrinks and reverses with doc length), PARTIAL; <strong>C192 REFUTED → PARTIAL</strong> (\"transfers for short docs, reverses for long\").</li><li>Equal-source weighting (statistician quick review 19:39) barely changes the pooled gap (+0.31% vs +0.42%; median source +0.04%).</li></ul><p>### Outside review 2026-11-22 20:07 (Haiku)</p><p><strong>Accepted:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>SQ214, the top pick:</strong> per-position loss bins plus an E1 SWA window sweep 64/256/1,024;</li><li>SQ215: a recurrence-free long-conv control;</li><li>SQ216: decoder-only noise floor before X1;</li><li>SQ217: weight EMA;</li><li>SQ218: the frozen test split as the confirmatory out-of-corpus set.</li></ul><p><strong>Design fixes:</strong></p><ul><li>X1 can't cache features (about 154 GB), so it recomputes on the fly on A1's deduplicated train;</li><li>X1 adds arm A″ (param-matched to the shared arm);</li><li><strong>RoPE is capped at max_seq_len = 1,024</strong>, so byte configs must raise it (forwarded to the byte-model builder).</li></ul><p>### Also in this version</p><ul><li>The hourly docs refresh (19:3x), which updated <code>notes/sketch.md</code>.</li><li>Quick reviews triaged: 19:25 skeptic (SQ213 cluster CI, in v0.4.65), 19:29 cheapest-experiment hunter (SQ189 scope extended), 19:34 newcomer (README fix and Start-here path, being applied by the site agent), 19:39 statistician (source weighting).</li></ul>"
