   "version": "v0.4.65",
   "title": "Byte Quest becomes a main quest (E12-E16); SQ99 cluster-robust re-analysis",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### Byte Quest: a main-quest arc (the human: \"add byte level tokens as a main quest, let's experiment with its granularity and loops\")</p><p><strong>Registered</strong> in <code>experiments/experiments.json</code> (arc \"Byte Quest (granularity x loops)\"), with cards and micro devlogs:</p><ul><li><strong>E12</strong> flat byte-level E1 (vocab 256, T = 4,096 bytes);</li><li><strong>E13</strong> patch-granularity sweep, P = 2/4/8, single-pass byte decoder;</li><li><strong>E14</strong> byte refinement-loop sweep, r = 1/2/4 shared vs an equal-FLOP unshared control (H-C2F);</li><li><strong>E15</strong> parallel-then-refine decoding within a patch (r &lt; P);</li><li><strong>E16</strong> the best decoder × looped global core × ternary global core.</li></ul><p><strong>Design</strong>: <code>notes/analysis-coarse-to-fine.md</code>. The primary metric is clean-val doc-level bits/char, plus exact-span accuracy (SQ209).</p><p><strong>Prerequisites</strong>: the SQ206 causality test, the SQ189 throughput probe, the flex-attention SWA patch (C12) and SQ207 (speller on frozen E1).</p><p><strong>In progress:</strong> a subagent is building the byte model family as staged patches (Phase 2b is running, so code paths can't change): byte dataset <code>code-py-v1-bytes</code>, causality tests, param/FLOP accounting, staged configs and <code>notes/byte-quest.md</code> with draft predictions. <strong>Predictions are registered before any run.</strong> ### SQ99 re-analysis (quick review 19:25, skeptical peer reviewer, Codex) The per-doc bootstrap ignored package clustering. From the saved per-doc NLL:</p><ul><li><strong>by-source cluster bootstrap 95% CI −0.13% to +1.03% (includes 0);</strong></li><li>leave-one-source-out +0.26% to +0.56% (the sign never flips);</li><li>E1 better on 14/31 sources.</li></ul><p><strong>The verdict DOES NOT TRANSFER stands</strong> (no evidence the in-corpus advantage carries out of corpus), <strong>but \"E1 is worse out of corpus\" is withdrawn.</strong> Recorded as a C192 limitation event; SQ213 done.</p>"
