   "version": "v0.4.61",
   "title": "Claim audit 2026-11-22-1902: 23 findings verified, 5 VERIFIED claims downgraded",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### Hourly claim audit 2026-11-22-1902 (AGENTS §0d-ter; first run)</p><p><strong>What</strong>: 8 read-only Codex GPT-6 Luna auditors ran in parallel over 48 claims (settled first), each in 1.5–3.7 min, with no failures. Verdicts: <strong>25 SOLID, 15 WEAK, 7 NEEDS-EVIDENCE, 1 WRONG.</strong> Every non-SOLID finding was checked against the primary files by a verifier subagent (Opus), then spot-checked by the main agent. All changes went in as ledger events through the API. Audit files with <code>## Triage</code> footers are in <code>notes/reviews/claims/2026-11-22-1902-b1…b8.md</code>.</p><p><strong>Downgrades:</strong></p><ul><li>VERIFIED → PARTIAL:</li><li><strong>C18</strong> (looping solves parity: n=2 seeds, and neg-eig GDN solves it in one pass);</li><li><strong>C8</strong> (compression ratio on contaminated val; exploratory n=1);</li><li><strong>C43</strong> (neg-eig parity: n=2 seeds);</li><li><strong>C44</strong> (2 seeds, 2 protocols);</li><li><strong>C100</strong> (harness wiring, tested on attention/SWA only).</li><li><strong>C127</strong> → UNVERIFIED: the PTX doc covers instructions only, and the Triton and FA3/FA4 compatibility parts were inferences.</li><li>C5, C6 and C92 are re-qualified as PARTIAL [exploratory n=1, K9-contaminated].</li><li>C108 and C22 stay REFUTED, with an exploratory tag.</li><li><strong>C15 → SUPERSEDED</strong> by <strong>C190</strong>. C15 bundled GDN (fixed memory, true) with SWA (K1: memory exponent 1.953, false). C190 states the GDN half alone, VERIFIED from K1.</li><li><strong>C107's misfiled K9 row</strong> was split out as <strong>C191</strong> (\"the val split is exact-dedup only\", VERIFIED from K9.json and <code>tools/prepare_data.py:9</code>); C107 reverted to PARTIAL.</li></ul><p><strong>Strengthened with pointers:</strong> C10, C3, C1 and C109 got evidence events and stay VERIFIED. C109 was re-read in the installed lm-eval 0.4.13 YAML.</p><p><strong>Auditor errors caught:</strong> C107's limit-8 eval JSON isn't empty (pass@1 0.875 on 8 of 2,555 problems). C108 → PARTIAL would contradict the policy, which keeps REFUTED.</p><p><strong>Result</strong>: claims-status is now <strong>18 VERIFIED (was 23), 20 PARTIAL, 6 REFUTED, 2 WRONG FOR OUR CODE, 72 UNVERIFIED, 1 SUPERSEDED; 119 claims.</strong> All 48 verdicts are recorded as <code>audit_verdict</code> events and in <code>claim-reviews.json</code>, putting those claims in their 6-hour cool-down (71 due next hour). Lint: 0 fail, 0 warn.</p><p><strong>Notes</strong>:</p><ul><li>The events carry version stamp v0.4.59 (the verifier's working version); they're committed here in v0.4.61.</li><li>The actor is <code>subagent:main-agent-verifier</code>, as the lint requires.</li><li>Unresolved: C104 needs the OpenCoder paper in refs; C127 needs a local probe.</li></ul><p>### Quick review 19:16 (code-model practitioner, Codex) The repo-edit generate-and-test benchmark was rejected because it floors near 0 at 13M (C102). It's accepted in modified form as <strong>SQ210</strong>, a patch-likelihood probe on SQ99's out-of-corpus pool.</p>"
