   "version": "v0.4.59",
   "title": "Outside review 19:37: E0 may be a handicapped yardstick (init differs from Llama)",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### Outside review 2026-11-22 19:37 (Haiku, AGENTS §0d) <code>notes/reviews/2026-11-22-1937-review.md</code>, with the main agent's triage.</p><p><strong>Key finding:</strong> E0 may be a handicapped yardstick.</p><ul><li>E10 (HF Llama) has E0's exact params and FLOPs, the same step-0 loss and the same LR (3e-3), yet gets <strong>0.5822 / 0.5854 vs E0's 0.6063</strong> (seeds 0/1; contaminated val).</li><li><strong>Verified in code:</strong> E0 uses GPT-2-style scaled residual-output init (std 0.02/√(2·depth), <code>gogeta/model.py:246-248</code>); HF Llama uses a flat 0.02. Init is a plausible cause, not yet the established one.</li><li>The E0-parity criterion is evaluated in Q12 on E10's 3-seed mean and clean val; it isn't due yet.</li><li>Phase 2b's confirmatory comparison (H1) uses E10, not E0, so it's protected.</li><li><strong>SQ99's baseline is E0;</strong> it'll be re-run with the E10 checkpoint.</li></ul><p><strong>Accepted</strong> (new review range SQ200+):</p><ul><li><strong>SQ200 (top pick): an init-matched 2×2 swap of E0/E10 inits</strong> (~15–20 GPU-min);</li><li>SQ201: E1-vs-E10 horizon curve at a matched LR. E1 leads by 2.1% at 20M, and E10 leads by 0.4% at 200M (seed 0, contaminated);</li><li>SQ202: mixer-conversion test;</li><li>SQ203: per-token gain decomposition;</li><li>SQ204: an n-gram copy floor on the near-dup band (CPU).</li></ul><p><strong>Ordering adopted:</strong> SQ200 and SQ204 run right after Phase 2b, before the Q12 verdicts are written up. <strong>Rejected:</strong> \"Q9 wrongly marked done\". Its condition (LR_E10 ≠ 3e-3) is false, so skipping was correct. ### Quick review 19:09 (reproducibility auditor, Codex)</p><p><strong>Provenance audit done:</strong> K9's and SQ70's lint FAILs are lookup gaps (predictions were committed in their scripts before the results). <strong>K7-parity is a genuine pre-registration lapse:</strong> its script and results were first committed together in v0.4.12, so it's treated as exploratory. The fix is SQ205; the lint report gets regenerated with each science version.</p>"
