   "version": "v0.4.58",
   "title": "Claims ledger v2: immutable definitions + append-only events",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### Claims ledger redesign (the human's spec)</p><p><strong>What</strong> (a subagent built it; the main agent verified it): the ledger separates each claim's <strong>immutable definition</strong> from its <strong>evolving evidence</strong>.</p><ul><li><strong>Layout:</strong> one file per claim, <code>experiments/claims/ledger/C&lt;n&gt;.jsonl</code>.</li><li>Line 1 is the <code>created</code> event holding the definition: ID, proposition (verbatim), scope (dataset, architecture, model size, precision, hardware), type (empirical / theoretical / implementation / external finding / hypothesis), refutation criteria, dependencies, origin.</li><li>Every later line is an append-only event: evidence_added, status_change, limitation_added, audit_verdict, erratum, superseded. Each has a version, actor, evidence pointers and <code>verified_at</code> {commit, date}.</li><li>Status, evidence, limitations and \"last verified\" are <strong>derived</strong>.</li><li><strong>The immutability rule:</strong> the committed file must be an exact prefix of the working file.</li><li><strong>Writes go only through the API:</strong> <code>python experiments/claims_list.py add-event</code> / <code>new-claim</code>, with per-claim locks.</li><li><strong>Views:</strong> <code>experiments/claims/views/C&lt;n&gt;.md</code> and <code>experiments/claims-status.md</code>. The schema and rationale are in <code>experiments/claims/README.md</code>.</li><li><strong>Lint (<code>--check</code>, the release gate):</strong> required fields, the type enum, evidence pointers that exist on disk, last-verified, dependency cycles, dependents of refuted claims, the definition-immutability and append-only checks, and the seed rule for VERIFIED.</li><li><code>experiments/claims.md</code> is <strong>frozen</strong> as the v1 archive (only line 1 changed, to a frozen header; its sha256 is in <code>MIGRATION.json</code>).</li><li><code>claim_review_batches.py</code> also counts <code>audit_verdict</code> events toward the 6-hour cool-down.</li></ul><p><strong>Migration</strong> (<code>experiments/claims/migrate_v1.py</code>):</p><ul><li>117 IDs and 167 v1 rows → 167 events, matched 1:1 by <code>--verify</code>. 198 events in total.</li><li>Latest statuses are identical to v1: 23 VERIFIED, 14 PARTIAL, 6 REFUTED, 2 WRONG FOR OUR CODE, 72 UNVERIFIED.</li><li>Types: 56 external finding, 26 implementation, 18 hypothesis, 14 empirical, 3 theoretical (50 inferred, flagged).</li><li>49 limitations were added, quoted verbatim, with the source line checked.</li><li><strong>Gaps are left visible, not invented:</strong> \"TBD (not stated at creation)\" for scope (99–115 per field), refutation criteria (100) and dependencies (114).</li></ul><p><strong>Verified by the main agent</strong>:</p><ul><li><code>claims_list.py --check</code> exits 0 (lint 0 fail, 0 warn);</li><li><code>migrate_v1.py --verify</code>: 117 IDs, 167 rows, 167 events;</li><li>ledger tests pass (reported 15/15);</li><li><code>claim_review_batches.py status</code> works unchanged.</li></ul><p><strong>AGENTS.md</strong>: §0d-ter, §5 and §7 updated by the subagent; §0's \"source of truth\" line by the main agent. The audit brief now points auditors at the ledger files and views.</p><p><strong>Known issues</strong> (recorded, not hidden):</p><ul><li>C107 holds two different propositions (it needs a new ID for the K9 one);</li><li>C5's refutation criteria name E10 while its proposition names E0;</li><li><code>verified_at</code> for migrated rows is approximate;</li><li>the cockpit, <code>test_guard.py</code> and <code>repro/lint_science.py</code> still read the frozen v1 file (follow-ups).</li></ul><p><strong>Leak note</strong>: the release helper had staged in-progress versions of <code>claims_list.py</code> (v0.4.50/51) and a v2 view (v0.4.53) before the store existed. This version completes that state.</p>"
