   "html": "<p>### Run report forms (final hand-back; snapshot was v0.4.45)</p><p><strong>What</strong> (the human: \"I want to see the agent use the cockpit and fill out a form for each run... explains the experiment and its metadata and shows any useful graph\"):</p><ul><li><code>cockpit/runform.py</code> gives the cockpit draft, submit, render and list for forms.</li><li>MCP tools: <code>gogeta_run_form_draft</code>, <code>gogeta_run_form_submit</code> (state-changing; refuses empty narratives and claims cited without evidence pointers) and <code>gogeta_run_forms</code>. The MCP server now has 31 tools.</li><li>The TUI's Runs tab has a forms view, and <code>brief()</code> lists finished runs that have no form.</li><li><strong>Each form</strong> has machine-filled metadata (experiment and prediction, architecture, params and FLOPs, hyperparameters, commit, environment, metrics, the K9 data caveat, linked claims) and agent-written narrative fields. <strong>Charts</strong> are static SVGs, transparent so they work in dark mode, at most 9 KB each: loss vs tokens with val points, LR, grad norm, throughput, a sibling comparison (val vs LR for K7), and L(r) for E2.</li><li><strong>README:</strong> a \"Run report forms\" section explains how to view and fill forms.</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>15 of 15 finished runs have a form,</strong> filled <strong>by a subagent calling the cockpit's MCP server</strong> (82 MCP tool calls logged in the cockpit's SQLite, 0 failed). One refusal demo (empty purpose, claim evidence \"see above\") was refused and wrote nothing.</li><li>Cockpit tests: 35 + 22 unit tests OK, and the headless TUI check is FAILED: 0 twice. A flaky TUI wait was hardened, and tab keys stopping after a button click was fixed.</li></ul><p><strong>Flagged by the form-filling agent</strong> (from the run data; <strong>not a verdict</strong>: contaminated val, and the registered parity and C5 analyses wait for the 3-seed means on clean val):</p><ul><li><strong>E10 seed 0 (0.5822) is about 4% better than our E0 (0.6063)</strong> at identical shapes, which is outside the registered E0-parity tolerance;</li><li><strong>E10 at 3e-3 also edges out E1 at 3e-3 (0.5846)</strong> by 0.4%.</li></ul><p>Both bear directly on C5.</p><p><strong>Discrepancies noted on the forms</strong>: max grad-norm after step 300 from Trackio is 0.485/0.490, vs 0.38 in the micro devlogs; E1 reaches E0's final val at 172M tokens (form) vs 169M (devlog interpolation).</p>"
