   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p>### A2 statistics: Phase 2b analysis addendum (REGISTERED)</p><p><strong>What</strong>: rigor workstream A2 (statistics), from a subagent. <code>experiments/stats/core.py</code> covers paired/Welch CIs, effect sizes, BCa and paired bootstrap, sign-flip permutation, Holm/BH, TOST, variance components and MDE/power, with selftests including CI-coverage simulations. Also:</p><ul><li><code>replication_stats.py</code> (the secondary statistical layer over the Q6 discovery);</li><li><code>score_doclevel.py</code> (GPU: doc-level bits/char per checkpoint on the K9 clean and near-dup subsets);</li><li><code>pairing.md</code>;</li><li>the addendum, <strong>appended to <code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code></strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>The registered content</strong>:</p><ul><li>The original Phase 2b criteria stay the primary decision rule. They're now applied to the <strong>primary metric, doc-level bits/char on clean val</strong> (val docs with &lt; 80% 13-gram overlap with train: 2,333 docs; sensitivity at &lt; 50%). Training-time <code>val_loss</code> is secondary (K9).</li><li>The <strong>confirmatory family is fixed at m=2, Holm at 0.05</strong>: H1 E1 vs E10 (paired by seed; seed s fixes the data order, which is shared across architectures) and H2 E11 vs E1 (TOST with margin max(1%, 2 pooled sd)). Everything else is BH q=0.10 or descriptive. E2 vs E9 is n=1, descriptive.</li><li>A <strong>memorisation gap</strong> (near-dup minus clean bits/char) is reported per model. It's a caveat flag and never changes a verdict.</li><li><strong>Power at n=3:</strong> the MDE is about 2% at sd 0.004, so power for a 1.5% gap is about 0.55. The exact sign-flip test can't go below p=0.25 at n=3.</li></ul><p><strong>Registration timing (honest)</strong>: the addendum file was written at 18:30:17, before the first Phase 2b result (E10 seed 0, finished 18:31:38). It was committed a few minutes after that result existed. The main agent didn't open the result before committing, and an E10-only result can't inform H1 or H2.</p><p><strong>Open decisions (main agent)</strong>:</p><ul><li><code>score_doclevel.py</code> needs about 25 GPU-min after the campaign. It's queued, or the primary-metric verdicts stay INCOMPLETE.</li><li>A2 notes that the registered C5 rule (\"gap &gt; 2 pooled sd + separation\") is weaker than a 5% test. It's left unchanged, and the CI is reported beside it.</li><li>The retro-audit downgrades (C8, C18, C43) are pending the main agent's review, in the next version.</li></ul>"
