   "title": "Cockpit: TUI + MCP + SQLite logs + self-heal watchdog; evidence and micro-devlog rules",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong> (the human's requests: a TUI + MCP for the project; SQLite run and error logging; self-healing; \"be adaptive\"; every settled claim points to evidence; every experiment has a micro devlog). The cockpit was built by a subagent and verified by the main agent.</p><ul><li><strong><code>cockpit/</code></strong> (new top-level folder):</li><li><code>core.py</code> (stdlib; one JSON-returning function per question, incl. a ≤ 4 KB <code>brief()</code> for agents);</li><li><code>mcp_server.py</code>: <strong>28 MCP tools</strong>. Read-only ones: brief, status, queue, experiment, claims, search, runs, results, devlog, log tail, errors, incidents, SQL (SELECT-only). State-changing ones are confirm-gated: start/stop server, launch queue item, resolve error, incident update, resume campaign, watchdog;</li><li><code>tui.py</code> (Textual): 10 tabs, from Dashboard with a GPU card, campaign progress, CPU slots and server tiles with Start/Stop/Open, to Queue, Experiments, Claims, Devlog, Logs, Errors, Incidents, Runs and Search;</li><li><code>logdb.py</code>: the SQLite store at <code>~/fusiondance-data/cockpit/gogeta.sqlite</code> (data, never committed; tokens redacted on every write; incremental ingest of run folders, campaign logs, CPU jobs and tracebacks);</li><li><code>watchdog.py</code>: the self-heal daemon. It turns 15 kinds of fault (dead/hung runs, NaN/OOM/Triton errors, tracebacks, aborted campaigns, preflight REFUSED, failed CPU jobs, servers down, GPU ≥ 85 °C, low disk) into <strong>incidents</strong> with a context bundle and an agent brief. It does only safe recovery: server restarts with backoff, one retry for transient faults, a thermal pause, and resume-campaign files with exactly the unfinished items, auto-launched only for transient or thermal causes. It never edits code, deletes data or kills a healthy process.</li><li><strong>The venv</strong> <code>~/.venvs/gogeta-cockpit</code> (mcp 1.30.0, textual 8.2.8, pinned in <code>requirements-cockpit.txt</code>; ~81 MB) was installed under the human's TUI+MCP request. <code>.mcp.json</code> registers the server for Claude Code.</li><li><strong>Patches, unapplied</strong> (between campaigns): <code>notes/patches/cockpit-logging-<em>.patch</code> (launchers and trainer log straight to SQLite) and <code>cockpit-resilience-</em>.patch</code> (per-item campaign status and unfinished-item files; <code>--ckpt-every</code> / <code>--resume</code> for mid-run training resume, which is impossible today).</li><li><strong>AGENTS.md:</strong></li><li><strong>§0e</strong> cockpit first: one interface, SQLite logs;</li><li><strong>§0f</strong> self-heal: the detect → contain → triage → fix → test → version → push → resume → verify loop;</li><li><strong>§0g</strong> be adaptive: a gap is a cockpit bug, so extend it (pattern: one <code>core.py</code> function plus <code>expose(...)</code>), with <code>cockpit/BACKLOG.md</code> for known gaps;</li><li><strong>§5, new rules from the human:</strong> every settled ledger claim must cite a concrete evidence pointer, and every experiment keeps a micro devlog <code>experiments/devlogs/&lt;ID&gt;.md</code> (plan, launches, observations, incidents, deviations, results, decisions). A subagent is backfilling the devlogs and auditing evidence pointers.</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong> (re-run by the main agent):</p><ul><li><code>cockpit.sh --test</code>: <strong>48 tests OK</strong>, plus the TUI's headless check across all tabs with 0 failures;</li><li>MCP stdio probe: initialize OK, 28 tools listed, and 4 live calls returned without errors;</li><li>the subagent's live ingest: 14 runs, 42 events, 4 unresolved errors (the K7 preflight REFUSED lines);</li><li>no tokens or personal data in the committed files.</li></ul><p><strong>Not verified</strong>: the TUI driven by a human; <code>cockpit.ps1</code> in Windows Terminal; a long-running watchdog loop (it starts in the next step); the patches (only <code>git apply --check</code>).</p>"
