   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong> (control + science-cleanup agent, Phase 1; reviewed by the main agent):</p><ul><li><strong>Three wrong statements fixed everywhere they appeared</strong>, now matching the ledger and K1/K2:</li><li>C12 (sliding window \"O(n·w)\": our dense-mask kernel is O(n²)): <code>docs/index.html</code>, <code>README.md</code>, <code>site-src/learn.md</code>;</li><li>C13 (\"~10× smaller\" → computed 7.8× for the body, 3.1× for the whole model): <code>site-src/learn.md</code>;</li><li>C14 (\"ternary makes compute cheap\" → only with ternary kernels; ours are simulated): <code>docs/index.html</code>, <code>README.md</code>, writeups E3/E4.</li><li><strong><code>notes/science-gaps.md</code>:</strong> every known gap, its fix and its status. The six original gaps are fixed or designed. New ones found:</li><li>E1-vs-E0 \"matched compute\" is ambiguous (+4.4% params, −6% FLOPs; C95);</li><li>single-seed claims are stated as fact in the README and primer (left until the replication decides C5);</li><li><code>val_bits_per_char</code> bias ~0.05%;</li><li>train/val near-duplicate leakage unchecked;</li><li>one compute-budget violation (two out-of-launcher GPU jobs at ~17:05);</li><li>detached-run survival unverified.</li><li>No prediction was ever edited after the fact (checked against the registry's git history).</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>: n/a (docs). The site HTML is regenerated in v0.4.13.</p>"
