   "version": "v0.4.3",
   "title": "K4: Ternary gap vs model size",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong>: check K4 (Ternary gap vs model size): script, results JSON and card. Prediction committed in <code>f1b4ebd</code> before it ran.</p><p>### K4: Ternary gap vs model size</p><ul><li><strong>Question:</strong> Does the ternary quality gap shrink with size at our scale? (C17)</li><li><strong>Result:</strong> Mean relative gap <strong>15.32% / 13.76% / 10.55%</strong> at d = 64/128/256 (2 seeds, decreasing within each seed; <code>results/K4.json</code>).</li><li><strong>Verdict vs prediction:</strong> Hit on the trend; the gaps are larger than predicted (12/8/5%). Local analogue VERIFIED, so C17 is PARTIAL (3B parity untestable here).</li><li><strong>What it means:</strong> Ternary costs ~10%+ at tiny sizes; E3 should run at E1's tuned LR and be judged against this trend.</li><li><strong>Card:</strong> experiments/cards/K4.md</li></ul>"
