   "version": "v0.3.6",
   "title": "Research reviews, experiment cards + index, process rules",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Rules (AGENTS.md):</strong></li><li>§0b side quests;</li><li>§0c status updates every 10 minutes;</li><li>§5 compute budget (1 GPU job + ≤ 8 CPU jobs, 85 °C cool-down), launcher usage, a TRL venv and sandbox rule;</li><li>§6 one card per experiment plus a generated <code>experiments/INDEX.md</code>;</li><li>§1 <strong>every experiment of any kind is saved, version-tagged and gets its own devlog block</strong>, with the E-series reserved for the main thesis;</li><li>§1 <strong>no WIP commits: every commit is a tagged version</strong>.</li><li><strong>Experiment cards</strong> (<code>experiments/cards/</code>, from <code>_TEMPLATE.md</code>) for E0–E3, and <code>tools/build_experiment_index.py</code> (also run by <code>build_site_data.py</code>; supports <code>--registry</code> / <code>--tracked-only</code>).</li><li><strong>Research:</strong></li><li><code>notes/research-looped.md</code>: 12 looped-transformer papers, 2025–26;</li><li><code>notes/review-competitors.md</code>: fact-check of a pasted analysis on MixerLoop, Auron and TR-Mamba2-Attn;</li><li><code>notes/smollm2-reference.md</code>: SmolLM2-135M downloaded (rev <code>93efa2f</code>, sha256 matches the Hub, Apache-2.0) as an external sanity reference;</li><li>refs: <code>10-qwen</code> (Qwen3.8-Next architecture, FlashNext-RL, Qwen3) and <code>11-looped-2026</code> (12 papers).</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>: no training.</p><p><strong>Findings</strong>:</p><ul><li>\"Inkling 2\" is Thinking Machines' Inkling 2 Small: a mixture-of-experts transformer, not looped.</li><li>There's no Qwen4 paper on arXiv; Qwen3.8-Flash-Next is the official Qwen4 preview.</li><li>LT2 (2605.20670) already loops GDN hybrids, but no one combines loops with ternary weights.</li><li>The pasted analysis overstated MixerLoop (41.5% of the gain at 110M, not \"much\").</li><li>At matched FLOPs, loops lose on LM loss in every paper that checks.</li></ul><p><strong>Notes</strong>: the ledger and side-quest rows proposed by these reviews are committed with v0.4.6. The site isn't regenerated in this version, because its sources are mid-edit by the cleanup agent.</p><p><strong>History</strong>: unpushed untagged WIP commits made before the no-WIP rule: <code>f1b4ebd</code> (K1–K6 predictions), <code>4a3e361</code> (SQ6 prediction, compute rules), <code>21fb049</code> (launch scripts), <code>ea3aa5b</code> (TRL scaffold). Check results cite their hashes as provenance, so they stay.</p><p><strong>Next</strong>: one tagged version per check (v0.4.0–v0.4.6), then E11 registered.</p>"
