   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong></p><ul><li><strong>GitHub Pages enabled</strong>: legacy build from <code>main</code> / <code>docs</code>, HTTPS enforced. Live at <strong>https://monstercameron.github.io/Gogeta-0/</strong> and set as the repo's homepage link.</li><li><strong>All 7 version tags pushed</strong> (<code>v0.1.0</code> → <code>v0.3.2</code>). The repo now has <code>push.followTags = true</code>, so future pushes carry their annotated tags automatically.</li><li>README: \"Project site\" and \"Start here\" links point at the live site; new tags/site badges; the publishing section is now \"Project site\". <code>pyproject.toml</code> Homepage → the site, plus a Repository URL. AGENTS.md documents the remote, follow-tags and the post-push Pages check.</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>: first Pages build <code>built</code> in ~20 s. All key paths return HTTP 200 (landing, devlog, primer, E0/E2/E9 pages, CSS/JS, site data, banner). In the browser: version badge v0.3.2, 10 roadmap links resolve, E2's 2 charts render, no console errors.</p><p><strong>Next</strong>: unchanged. Training stays paused until the human asks; then E9 and the seed replications (detached).</p>"
