   "title": "Plain-English experiment pages and a newcomer primer",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong></p><ul><li><strong>One page per experiment</strong> on the site (<code>docs/experiments/E0–E9.html</code>), generated from <code>experiments/writeups/E&lt;n&gt;.md</code>. Each opens with <strong>\"What it means, in plain English\"</strong>, then the setup, charts, a breakdown of the findings, the prediction scorecard, caveats and next steps. Planned experiments get a short \"what it will test\" page.</li><li><strong>\"Start here\" primer</strong> (<code>docs/learn.html</code> from <code>site-src/learn.md</code>): how a model learns, every number on the site decoded (loss, perplexity, bits/char, FLOPs, seeds), the three tricks as analogies, and what we've found so far.</li><li><strong>Charts:</strong> interactive learning curves and loss-vs-loops (hover crosshair/tooltips, legend, direct labels, \"show the numbers\" tables) from <code>experiments/curves/E&lt;n&gt;.json</code>. The palette was validated for colour-blind safety on the site's dark surfaces.</li><li><strong>AGENTS.md rule:</strong> every finished experiment gets its write-up, curve file and generated page before its version is cut.</li><li>Devlog cards and roadmap items link to the experiment pages; \"Start here\" is in every nav.</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>: no training (paused by request). Yardsticks measured on CPU for the explainers: the models compress held-out Python to ~3% of its size vs 15.4% for <code>xz -9</code> and 25.1% for <code>gzip -9</code>; E1 reached E0's final quality at 84% of the training budget.</p><p><strong>Findings / surprises</strong></p><ul><li>⚠ <strong>The replication queue was killed</strong> when the previous agent session ended (E9 at step 600, E2-s1 at step 200). There are no new results, E9 is back to <code>planned</code>, and the replication predictions stay open. Future queues should run detached (<code>nohup</code>/<code>setsid</code>).</li><li><strong>Correction to v0.3.0:</strong> E2's scorecard is <strong>5 of 7</strong> predicted claims, not \"5 of 8\".</li></ul><p><strong>Next</strong>: when training resumes: E9, then seeds 1–2 (detached), then the functional-correctness eval.</p>"
